// §14 entry 24 -- an implementation whose mark exceeds the trait's declared
// ceiling, reached ONLY through a generic, never boxed -> EXS-E0510.
//
// This entry exists because the rule it tests did not. §4.4 stated its
// exceeds-check only for `dyn` construction, so an implementation reached
// solely through a generic `<T: Trait>` was checked against nothing.
// prototypes/gendict/ demonstrated the hole by running code; §4.4 now makes a
// trait's declared rows a ceiling on EVERY implementation, boxed or not.
//
// The violation is NOT that Right is internally inconsistent -- it declares
// the `rete` its body uses. It is that Right's mark exceeds what
// Summable.combine declares, which is the only fact `total` had to trust when
// it declared `poscit alloc`.
//
// Nothing here ever writes `dyn`. That is the point.
//
// FIXED, found by running: bare `self` (no type) does not parse. §8.6
// decision 8 spends no keyword on the receiver -- "There is no `self`, no
// `Self`, no receiver syntax" -- so `self` is an ordinary parameter name
// and, like every other `Param ::= IDENT ':' Type`, needs its own type:
// the interface's own name (`Summable`) in the interface, meaning "the
// implementing type," and the concrete type (`Right`) in the impl. The
// original `combine(self, other: f32)` read as `self` immediately
// followed by `,` with no `:` -- `EXS-E0201` at both signatures, confirmed
// by `exsc aedifica --emitte ast` before this fix, not assumed from the
// grammar alone. Same defect §14 entry 12's fixture had (checker.md
// finding 6); the fix here is the same shape.
//
// FIXED, three more found by running (a fresh `exsc` from the working tree,
// `--diagnostica json`, this file with `self`'s type already corrected):
//
//   - the fixture never declared `structura Right` at all -- used as the
//     impl target and as `self`'s type, declared nowhere, which raised its
//     own `EXS-E0301` at both uses independently of anything below. Added
//     above with one plain field: the mark this entry tests is the impl
//     HEAD's own declared row (`poscit alloc, rete` on line 41), never a
//     struct's computed field mark (spec §4.3), so `Right` needs no
//     capability-typed field of its own to make the point.
//   - `ast/from_cst.inc`'s `__ast_w_iface` (the implementation branch) gave
//     `AST_D_IMPL` the TRAIT's own last-segment name (`Summable`) instead of
//     no name at all, contradicting the invariant `resolve.inc`'s
//     `__chk_mods` states immediately above the check it tripped ("an
//     `Impl` head introduces no name"): `interfacies Summable in Right
//     poscit alloc, rete { ... }` collided with `Summable`'s own
//     declaration -- a spurious `EXS-E0302`. Fixed in `from_cst.inc`;
//     pinned by `tests/unit/ast_from_cst_impl_noname.asm`.
//   - `resolve.inc`'s `.fn_open:` read `Fn.a` (signature) and `Fn.b` (body)
//     but never `Fn.c` (`Generics`), so `total<T: Summable>`'s OWN `T` was
//     never bound into its frame and fell through to a module-scope miss --
//     a spurious `EXS-E0301` at `T`'s use in `(a: T, ...)`. Fixed by walking
//     `Fn.c` into the `CHK_FR_FN` frame before the signature, reusing
//     `.genparam:`'s existing single-parameter binder; pinned by
//     `tests/unit/chk_genparam_fn_bind.asm`.
//
// RESOLVED, and the record of how. The measured code set moved
// {EXS-E0301, EXS-E0302, EXS-E0510} -> {EXS-E0303, EXS-E0510} ->
// {EXS-E0510}. The middle state stood for one wave and the `EXS-E0303` in it
// was diagnosed here as "whatever computes the resulting CALL's type does not
// yet resolve to `f32`". That reading was wrong in its location, and worth
// keeping so the next person does not re-derive it: the code was NOT at the
// call's result. It was at `a`, the RECEIVER, and it came from
// `__chk_ty_call`'s `.args:` comparing parameter 0 by identity.
// `__chk_ty_method`'s `.bound:` arm falls through into `.iface:`, so a
// `T: Summable` receiver finds `combine` on the INTERFACE, whose parameter 0
// is spelled `Summable` -- meaning "the implementing type" (§8.6 decision 8:
// no `self`, no `Self`). Comparing `T` against `Summable` is comparing a type
// parameter against the interface that bounds it, which is exactly what
// checker.md section 2.7 calls correct resolution. The call's type WAS `f32`
// all along; `tests/unit/chk_ty_method_bound.asm`'s row b01 pins that
// separately, because "no diagnostic" would also be the answer of a checker
// that had given up on the call.
//
// Fixed by skipping that one comparison when the receiver's own type kind is
// `AST_TY_PARAM` or `AST_TY_DYN` -- one guard, one cause, both kinds.
// `EXS-E0510` fires exactly where and only where §4.4 says it should, as it
// did through every one of those three states.
//
// Measured with a fresh `exsc` from the working tree, `--diagnostica json`,
// against THIS file: `{EXS-E0510}`, once, at the implementation head
// `interfacies Summable in Right poscit alloc, rete` -- which is §4.4's
// ceiling check on an implementation reached only through a generic, the rule
// this entry exists for. `status=run`.

// TEST: entry=24 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0510 status=run

interfacies Summable {
    functio combine(self: Summable, other: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc
}

functio usa_rete(x: f32) -> f32 poscit rete {
    redde x;
}

structura Right { n: mensura }

interfacies Summable in Right poscit alloc, rete {
    functio combine(self: Right, other: f32) -> f32 {
        redde usa_rete(other);
    }
}

publica functio total<T: Summable>(a: T, b: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc {
    redde a.combine(b);
}
